DESCRIPTION:World Freedom Day falls on November 9\, the anniversary of the 
 night in 1989 when East Germany opened the Berlin Wall. It is a United Sta
 tes observance created by presidential proclamation in 2001\, not a federa
 l holiday\, and presidents of both parties have issued it since. The date 
 was chosen for a specific reason\, and the reason is slightly uncomfortabl
 e: the Wall's opening was less a decision carried out on schedule than an 
 announcement that got away from the government that made it.\n\nhttps://to
 daycelebrates.com/holiday/world-freedom-day/
